<title>ITALY: Mediobanca launches bond on Monday.</title>
<headline>Mediobanca launches bond on Monday.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian merchant bank Mediobanca said in a statement on Friday that it was launching a one trillion lire two-year zero coupon bond with a net yield of 6.84 percent.</p>
<p>The bonds will be repayable at par on September 6, 1998 and are to be quoted on the Milan bourse. They are being issued in five million lire tranches at a price of 4.304 million lire.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
